# Google’s ads.txt crawler must get a plain-text file at /ads.txt.
# auto-trailing-slash would otherwise 404 /ads.txt/ through the Worker.
/ads.txt/ /ads.txt 301

# No www → apex rule here, on purpose. Workers Static Assets validates the
# *source* of a `_redirects` line with `onlyRelative`, so an absolute
# `https://www.…/*` source is rejected (Cloudflare API error 100324) and takes
# the whole deploy down with it — the destination may be absolute, the source
# may not. Rewriting it relative does not help either: a `/*` source matches
# the apex too and would 301 it to itself.
#
# Hostname canonicalization has to sit above the asset layer. Add a zone-level
# Redirect Rule in the Cloudflare dashboard instead:
#   www.freeresumebuilder.co.in/*  →  https://freeresumebuilder.co.in/${1}  (301)
# It matches on hostname, runs at the edge, and costs no Worker invocations —
# unlike doing it in workers/index.ts, which would need `run_worker_first`
# widened past /api/* and would bill every page view against the free plan.
#
# Until that rule exists, the canonical tag is what points crawlers at the apex.
